+### Transferring a user between organizations
+
+`POST /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}/transfer` moves a user (for example between
+group companies) to the organization named in `toOrgId`.
+
+- The caller must belong to `{orgID}` (otherwise 404) and be an org admin of it
+  (otherwise 403). The user must belong to `{orgID}` (otherwise 404).
+- `toOrgId` must be a known organization (otherwise 400), and must differ from
+  the user's current one (otherwise 400).
+- The user's project memberships in the old organization are removed, and tasks
+  assigned to them in those projects are unassigned, so the model rules keep
+  holding. The org admin flag does not carry over.
+- The change is atomic. The caller's rights in the target organization are not
+  checked: only admins of the source organization can transfer a user out.
+
